    "content": "The Czech Republic (Czechia) is a landlocked Central European nation with a population of over 10 million, featuring Prague as its capital and largest city. Known for its rich history, castles, and beer culture, it is a parliamentary democracy, a member of the EU and NATO, and shares borders with Germany, Poland, Slovakia, and Austria. Key Information Capital: Prague (Praha) Official Language: Czech Currency: Czech Koruna (CZK) Major Cities: Prague, Brno, Ostrava, Plzeň (Pilsen) Regions: Bohemia, Moravia, and Silesia Key Facts Geography: Located in Central Europe, the country is characterized by rolling hills and mountains. History: Formed as an independent state on January 1, 1993, following the peaceful dissolution of Czechoslovakia. Culture: Famous for its, 2,000+ castles, beer (origin of Pilsner), and rich musical history. Visitor Information: As part of the Schengen Area, many travelers can enter without a visa for short stays, though it is recommended to check official Ministry of Foreign Affairs guidelines. Ministry of Foreign Affairs Political Structure: Parliamentary republic with a President as head of state and Prime Minister as head of government.",
